id: pm-web-6ama
title: Refresh proxy-addr lockfile to clear the critical production audit advisory
description: Release preflight reports GHSA-jqcg-44mw-7w3h in locked proxy-addr 2.0.7. Registry offers compatible 2.0.8. Validate the minimal transitive lockfile refresh with the public package release gates; deployment remediation is separate.
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-07T21:50:18.097Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-07T22:17:07.473Z"
author: codex-sol
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-07T21:51:45.454Z",codex-sol,"Release preflight reproduced GHSA-jqcg-44mw-7w3h with proxy-addr 2.0.7. A minimal npm update proxy-addr --ignore-scripts refresh changes only that transitive lockfile resolution to 2.0.8. No dependency ranges, gate thresholds or hosted resources change; validating with both release runners."
  "2026-10-07T22:16:59.754Z",codex-sol,"Close-ready: locked proxy-addr is now 2.0.8, and npm run audit:prod reports zero production vulnerabilities. Both full release gates pass, including packed npm/Bun acceptance. The lockfile refresh changes no dependency range or gate threshold. Existing development-audit work remains separate; no hosted remediation is claimed."
